CSS grid for AnkiNX (shared decks lay out word tables and option lists with
it): litehtml has no grid, so display:grid showed as one column. Adds
render_item_grid (display: grid / inline-grid) for the common subset:
grid-template-columns (lengths, %, fr, auto, repeat() with a count or
auto-fill/auto-fit, minmax()), items placed row by row (grid-column: N,
span N, N / M; grid-column-start/-end), gap/grid-gap/column-gap/row-gap,
rows as tall as their tallest item, align-items/-self, justify-items/-self
and place-items/-self. Grid items are blockified like flex items. Not
covered: grid-template-rows/-areas, grid-row, dense packing.

